Package: hd-secboot
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, openssl, efitools, sbsigntool
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian Secure Boot keys
 Installs and keeps installed the tools to sign EFI files with Secure Boot
 keys of the owner of the system and to enroll those keys in the firmware:
 openssl, efitools and sbsigntool.
 .
 On its first installation it generates the keys in /etc/hyprdebian/secboot:
 a platform key (PK), a key exchange key (KEK) and a signature database key
 (db), each with its certificate, EFI signature list and signed update.
 Existing keys are never replaced. hd-secboot-enroll enrolls them in the
 firmware.
